  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 123 AM MST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nToday through Sun night...Upper level low in northern NV will \nbecome an open wave, then move through southern Idaho by early \nevening tonight. This is bringing some light to moderate \nprecipitation to all locations except the central Idaho \nmountains, where it will be very light, if any. The rain and \nsnowfall continues in the eastern half of the forecast area \novernight into Sat morning, and in the upper Snake Highlands \ninto the afternoon and Sat evening. By Sun, a shortwave is \nejected from an eastern Pacific low off the OR-WA coast and by \nSun morning light precipitation will be developing over the \nnorthern half of the forecast area in a warm overrunning \npattern. The deep southwest flow continues to develop \nprecipitation in the central Idaho mountains and southern \nhighlands on Sun night as well. \n\nTemperatures will continue the afternoon rain-overnight and\nmorning snow with very little change from one day to the next in\nthis period. Lows in the teens and twenties, and highs in the\nthirties and lower 40s. \n\nGusty wind expected today and tonight, mostly in the Snake River\nplain and eastern Magic Valley. Otherwise, light wind during\nthis near term period.\n\nMon through Thanksgiving Day...Embedded shortwave expected on \nMon that should bring a heightened chance of precipitation shows\nup in all clusters to varying degrees of amplitude. Tue has a \nhigh amplitude upper level ridge as another closed low moves \ninto the eastern Pacific. A weaker trough appears to be \napproaching on Wed which may bring more precipitation, and the \nThanksgiving day appears to have another weak upper level ridge\nwith axis directly over Idaho. NBM guidance though indicates a\nslight chance of precipitation on the holiday even though none\nof the clusters appear to indicate any precipitation.",
